{
  "explanation": "The attacker originating from IP 45.9.148.201 utilized the Zgrab network scanner to perform automated reconnaissance by probing for sensitive configuration files, version control metadata, and administrative endpoints like '.env', '.git/HEAD', and AWS credentials. The HTTP 404 status codes returned indicate that these specific resources were not found on the server, meaning this initial scanning phase was unsuccessful in immediately exposing sensitive files.",
  "mitre_tactic": "Reconnaissance",
  "recommended_actions": [
    "Block the source IP address 45.9.148.201 at the firewall or WAF level to prevent further probing.",
    "Ensure sensitive files and directories (such as .git, .env, and cloud credentials) are excluded from web root deployment.",
    "Implement rate limiting and automated IP banning for clients generating excessive 404 errors over a short duration."
  ]
}
